{"id":33102,"slug":"kalpana","title":"Kalpana","year":1948,"country":"India","duration":152,"spine":1148,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/33102-kalpana","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/0c4c61e5d8e55d2ffa2f60713f3b98a8/5BN1ZGP13Lzxm2DBUh0vwIAGvzoakS_large.jpg","description":"The only film by the visionary dancer and choreographer Uday Shankar is a utopian dream of cultural renewal and a celebration of Indian dance in all its variety. Unfolding as an epic film within a film, Kalpana tells the story of a dancer (the director himself) who is determined to open a cultural center and breathe new life into India’s traditional artistic forms. Meanwhile, the visible adoration between him and his lead dancer arouses the jealousy of his enterprising companion. A riot of ecstatic imagery—including swirling surrealist dance spectacles—is interwoven with anticolonial, anticapitalist commentary, making for a radical, proto-Bollywood work that is one of the most influential films in Indian cinema.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Uday Shankar","slug":"uday-shankar"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Uday Shankar","role":"Udayan, film director","slug":"uday-shankar"},{"actor":"Amala Uday Shankar","role":"Uma","slug":"amala-uday-shankar"},{"actor":"Lakshmi Kanta","role":"Kamini","slug":"lakshmi-kanta"},{"actor":"Dr. Glv. Subbarao","role":"Drawing master","slug":"dr-glv-subbarao"},{"actor":"Birendra Banerjee","role":"Noor","slug":"birendra-banerjee"},{"actor":"Swaraj Mitter Gupta","role":"Ramesh","slug":"swaraj-mitter-gupta"},{"actor":"Anil Kumar Chopra","role":"Madan, schoolteacher","slug":"anil-kumar-chopra"},{"actor":"Brijo Behari Banerjee","role":"Uma’s father","slug":"brijo-behari-banerjee"},{"actor":"Chiranjilal Shah","role":"Gope","slug":"chiranjilal-shah"},{"actor":"Devilal Samar","role":"Sundar","slug":"devilal-samar"},{"actor":"K. Mukerjee","role":"Grandfather","slug":"k-mukerjee"},{"actor":"Dulal Sen","role":"Mama","slug":"dulal-sen"},{"acto